---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/indas/indas116.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope & Definitions" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Identifying a Lease" },
        { id: "s4", label: "The Single Lessee Model — Right-of-Use Asset & Lease Liability" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Recognition Exemptions" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Lessor Accounting" },
        { id: "s7", label: "The COVID-19 Rent Concession Practical Expedient — Indian Timeline" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Sale and Leaseback" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Ind AS 116 vs IFRS 16 — Full Comparison" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <!-- ============ SECTION 1 — CONCEPTUAL FRAMEWORK LINKAGE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Identical single-model philosophy to IFRS 16</div>
        <div class="principle">Ind AS 116 applies the IDENTICAL principle as IFRS 16 — nearly ALL leases are brought ON-BALANCE-SHEET for lessees via a right-of-use asset and lease liability, eliminating the old operating vs finance lease distinction for lessees (Ind AS 17's dual model).</div>
        <div class="elabel">HOW IND AS 116 MAPS TO THE FRAMEWORK</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span><strong style="font-weight:500">Faithful representation</strong> — reflecting the genuine economic obligation of committed lease payments — identical to IFRS 16</span>
          <span><strong style="font-weight:500">Comparability</strong> — eliminating the prior ability to structure leases as "off-balance-sheet" operating leases — identical to IFRS 16</span>
          <span><strong style="font-weight:500">India's own COVID-19 practical expedient</strong> — the MCA introduced an Ind AS 116 amendment permitting a practical expedient for COVID-19-related rent concessions, closely mirroring IFRS 16's own equivalent amendment in SUBSTANCE, though introduced through India's own separate notification process and timeline</span>
        </div>
        <div class="note">Ind AS 116 REPLACED the earlier Ind AS 17, identical in effect to how IFRS 16 replaced IAS 17 globally — a major transition requiring most Indian lessees to bring OPERATING leases onto the balance sheet for the first time.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">The core mechanics — identical to IFRS 16</div>
        <div class="formula-box"><div class="f-eq">Right-of-use asset = Initial lease liability + prepayments + initial direct costs − incentives received</div></div>
        <div class="callout info callout--chip" style="margin-bottom:0;">ℹ️ IDENTICAL initial measurement formula to IFRS 16.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 2 — SCOPE & DEFINITIONS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope &amp; Applicability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">What Ind AS 116 covers</div>
        <div class="principle">Ind AS 116 applies to ALL leases except leases of intangible assets, biological assets, service concession arrangements, licences of IP, and rights under Ind AS 115-scoped arrangements — IDENTICAL scope to IFRS 16.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Key definitions you must know</div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Right-of-use asset</div><div class="glossary-def">IDENTICAL definition to IFRS 16 — an asset representing a lessee's right to use an underlying asset over the lease term.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">MCA</div><div class="glossary-def">Ministry of Corporate Affairs — the Indian government body that notifies Ind AS amendments, including the COVID-19 rent concession expedient.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 3 — IDENTIFYING A LEASE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Identifying a Lease</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Identical control-based test to IFRS 16</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A contract is/contains a lease if it conveys the RIGHT TO CONTROL the use of an identified asset for a period in exchange for consideration — IDENTICAL to IFRS 16, requiring both the right to obtain substantially all economic benefits AND the right to direct use.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 4 — SINGLE LESSEE MODEL ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>The Single Lessee Model — Right-of-Use Asset &amp; Lease Liability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Identical recognition, measurement, and subsequent accounting to IFRS 16</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;">
          <div class="wk-title">Example 1: An Indian retailer's store lease</div>
          <div class="wk-body">An Indian retail company enters a 5-year store lease with annual payments of ₹24,00,000, and an incremental borrowing rate of 10%.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The lease liability is recognised at the PRESENT VALUE of the 5 annual payments discounted at 10% (approximately ₹90,98,000), with an EQUAL right-of-use asset recognised initially — the asset is then depreciated on a straight-line basis, while the liability accretes interest and is reduced by payments — an IDENTICAL mechanism to how IFRS 16 would account for the same lease globally.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 5 — RECOGNITION EXEMPTIONS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Recognition Exemptions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Identical two exemptions to IFRS 16</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Short-term leases (12 months or less, no purchase option) and low-value asset leases — IDENTICAL exemptions to IFRS 16, permitting straight-line expense recognition instead of balance sheet recognition.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 6 — LESSOR ACCOUNTING ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Lessor Accounting</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Identical dual model to IFRS 16</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Lessors continue to classify leases as OPERATING or FINANCE, largely UNCHANGED from the old Ind AS 17 lessor model — IDENTICAL to IFRS 16's own retained lessor approach.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 7 — COVID-19 RENT CONCESSION ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>The COVID-19 Rent Concession Practical Expedient — Indian Timeline</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">A genuinely notable, though narrow, Indian-specific procedural difference</div>
        <div class="principle">Both the IASB (for IFRS 16) and India's MCA (for Ind AS 116) introduced a practical expedient allowing lessees to elect NOT to assess whether a COVID-19-related rent concession is a lease modification, instead accounting for it directly in profit or loss. While CLOSELY MIRRORING each other in substance, the Indian amendment was notified through India's own separate rule-making process (Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Amendment Rules) with its own specific effective date and scope wording, rather than being automatically incorporated the moment the IASB issued its equivalent amendment.</div>
        <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;">
          <div class="wk-title">Example 2: Applying the rent concession expedient</div>
          <div class="wk-body">An Indian retail tenant receives a ₹3,00,000 rent waiver from its landlord as a direct consequence of COVID-19, with no other substantive contractual terms changed.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">Under the Ind AS 116 practical expedient, the tenant may elect to recognise the ₹3,00,000 as a REDUCTION of lease expense/liability directly in profit or loss WITHOUT reassessing whether this constitutes a lease modification — an IDENTICAL practical outcome to how IFRS 16's own equivalent expedient would apply, though arising from India's own separately notified amendment rather than automatic global incorporation.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 8 — SALE AND LEASEBACK ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Sale and Leaseback</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Identical to IFRS 16</div>
        <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">Sale and leaseback transactions are assessed against Ind AS 115's control transfer criteria to determine whether a genuine sale has occurred — IDENTICAL to IFRS 16's own cross-reference approach.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 9 — DISCLOSURE ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Identical disclosure requirements to IFRS 16</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Right-of-use asset depreciation, interest expense on lease liabilities</span>
          <span>Short-term/low-value lease expense</span>
          <span>Maturity analysis of lease liabilities</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 10 — JUDGMENTS & ESTIMATES ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where management judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Determining the lease term (including renewal/termination option assessments)</span>
              <span>Whether a rent concession genuinely qualifies for the COVID-19 practical expedient</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Incremental borrowing rate, particularly for Indian entities without an easily observable rate</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout warn" style="margin-top:8px;margin-bottom:0;">⚠️ Determining an appropriate incremental borrowing rate can be genuinely challenging for Indian unlisted/smaller entities without direct market borrowing rate references, often requiring build-up approaches referencing risk-free rates plus credit spread adjustments.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 11 — IND AS 116 VS IFRS 16 ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Ind AS 116 vs IFRS 16 — Full Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comprehensive comparison table</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 16</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-success);">Ind AS 116</span></div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Single lessee on-balance-sheet model</span><span>Standard model</span><span>IDENTICAL — no substantive divergence</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Recognition exemptions</span><span>Short-term, low-value</span><span>IDENTICAL</span></div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>COVID-19 rent concession expedient</span><span>IASB amendment, global effective date</span><span>MCA's own SEPARATELY notified amendment, closely mirroring IFRS 16's substance but on India's own notification timeline</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Predecessor standard replaced</span><span>IAS 17</span><span>Ind AS 17</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">Ind AS 116 is essentially IDENTICAL to IFRS 16 in substance — the meaningful Indian divergence is a narrow, procedural difference in how the COVID-19 rent concession practical expedient was notified, not any accounting divergence.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 12 — STATEMENT MAPPING ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Comprehensive event-to-statement mapping table</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event / transaction</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Right-of-use asset depreciation</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> <span class="badge bs">Balance Sheet</span></span><span>Identical to IFRS 16</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Lease liability interest accretion</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> <span class="badge bs">Balance Sheet</span></span><span>Identical to IFRS 16</span></div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>COVID-19 rent concession (elected)</span><span><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Direct reduction, no modification reassessment</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 13 — RELATED STANDARDS ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>IFRS 16</span><span>The global counterpart standard, near-identically converged</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Ind AS 17 (withdrawn)</span><span>Predecessor standard replaced by Ind AS 116</span></div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Ind AS 115</span><span>Supplies the control transfer test for sale and leaseback</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Quick-reference glossary</div>
        <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Incremental borrowing rate</div><div class="glossary-def">The rate a lessee would have to pay to borrow funds to obtain an asset of similar value in a similar economic environment — identical concept to IFRS 16.</div></div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Amendment Rules</div><div class="glossary-def">The MCA's mechanism for notifying Ind AS amendments, including the COVID-19 rent concession expedient.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 14 — GLOSSARY ============ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <Glossary entries={[
      { term: "Right-of-use asset", definition: "An asset representing a lessee's right to use an underlying asset over the lease term — IDENTICAL definition to IFRS 16." },
      { term: "Lease liability", definition: "The lessee's obligation to make lease payments, measured at the present value of lease payments — IDENTICAL definition to IFRS 16." },
      { term: "Incremental borrowing rate", definition: "The rate a lessee would have to pay to borrow funds to obtain an asset of similar value in a similar economic environment — identical concept to IFRS 16." },
      { term: "COVID-19 rent concession expedient", definition: "A practical expedient permitting lessees to elect not to assess whether a COVID-19-related rent concession is a lease modification, instead accounting for it directly in profit or loss." },
    ]} />

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
